TASK-200 runtime harness: main-queue heartbeat during an upgrade recompile of
all four filter lists and during a mid-session list update, before and after
moving rule serialisation and the bad-rule search off the main queue.
Temporary code, never committed to Detour/. It is TASK-199's harness
(docs/harness/task199-harness.patch, renamed Task199 -> Task200) plus:
  - the list URLProtocol answers with the ETag in <lists>/<id>.etag when that
    file exists (else "v2"), so a list can "change upstream";
  - DETOUR_VERIFY_WAIT_COUNT=<id>=<n>,... waits until those lists' compiled
    rule counts reach n (an update download compiled mid-session);
  - "OPEN <host>" is logged before each test tab is created, and the closing
    heartbeat line lists every gap over 250 ms;
  - "PARSE START/END <id> (cache|download)" around each parser.parse call in
    ContentBlockerManager (the one hunk outside Detour/App/), and the app's
    phys_footprint with its lifetime peak (task_vm_info) after the recompile
    wait and before "done".

    SP=<scratch>; mkdir -p $SP/www $SP/out $SP/lists
    # www/: page.html + jquery.popunder.js as in TASK-199's header.
    # lists/<id>.txt: the four filter list texts (TASK-199's copies).
    python3 -m http.server 8899 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory $SP/www &
    /usr/bin/log stream --style compact --level info --predicate \
        'subsystem == "com.detourbrowser.mac" AND category == "content-blocker"' > $SP/out/oslog.txt &
    git apply docs/harness/task200-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug build -derivedDataPath .derived
    DETOUR_DATA_DIR=DetourVerify200 DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR=$SP/out DETOUR_VERIFY_PORT=8899 \
        DETOUR_VERIFY_LISTS=<lists dir> DETOUR_VERIFY_RUN=<name> \
        [DETOUR_VERIFY_WAIT_FORMAT=1] [DETOUR_VERIFY_WAIT_COUNT=easylist=78191,easylist-cookie=25023] \
        .derived/Build/Products/Debug/Detour.app/Contents/MacOS/Detour &
    # wait for "done" in out/verify-<name>.log, kill that pid
    git apply -R docs/harness/task200-harness.patch && xcodegen generate

Scenarios (defaults suite com.detourbrowser.mac.DetourVerify200, never the
real com.detourbrowser.mac; data dir ~/Library/Application Support/DetourVerify200):
- upgrade: ContentBlocker/<id>.txt = the list texts; ContentRuleLists/ =
  TASK-199's old-parser compiled lists; every list lastFetch now, etag "v2",
  NO rulesFormat key (all four recompile from cache at launch); as in
  TASK-199's run 2, easylist-cookie.txt deleted (unconditional fallback
  fetch, then its 2-bad-rule search) and urlhaus-filter etag "v1" with
  lastFetch two days ago (refresh compiles after its cache compile).
  Run with WAIT_FORMAT=1.
- relaunch: the same data dir again (lists reused, nothing compiled).
- update: after the upgrade, a lists dir where easylist.txt and
  easylist-cookie.txt have one rule more and <id>.etag = "v3"; their
  lastFetch set two days ago (etag "v2"), so refreshIfNeeded downloads (200)
  and compiles both mid-session. Run with
  WAIT_COUNT=easylist=78191,easylist-cookie=25023.
Check the screen is unlocked before and after each run (a locked screen
stops the heartbeat). For attribution, `sample <pid> 19 1 -mayDie` started
2 s after launch (sandbox off; sampling from exec time records nothing).

